# Deep-understanding rollout progress

This directory configures the central deterministic five-gate report for
Mathematics, Physics, Chemistry, Biology and Economics. Current work targets
Chemistry only; the achieved Mathematics, Physics and Biology M7 floors remain protected.

Current Chemistry continuation (18 October):
[Chemistry final integration progress](../../../../../docs/qa-ci/chemie-current450-final-integration-progress-2026-10-18.md).
The latest complete standard central report measures **450/450 curricular-atomic
Chemistry goals** at all five strict D/P/A/M/V gates, with CQR-303 passing all
six required checks. Actual source/course checks CQR-003 and CQR-004 also pass,
with no unsupported assignments, reverse source gaps or course mismatches.
These results do **not** establish M7: the complete report currently assigns
Chemistry **M2** because its Sek-II route profile has **77 missing motivation
paths, 107 missing terminal paths and 10 draft assessment releases**. The
protected Chemistry M6 floor correctly fails until these real route and
assessment duties are resolved. No floor or route scope has been reduced.

Since that complete measurement, actual paired assessment reviews have been
integrated for ten existing exams. The unchanged finite route evaluator now
initially measured **105 missing terminal paths** and **two HE exam-interface
holds**. Those two admission interfaces subsequently passed independent
current checks and are integrated as well: the actual unchanged route
evaluator now measures **103 missing terminal paths** and **zero incomplete
releases among the 32 existing endpoints**; motivation still has 77 missing
paths. Two recovered local endpoints
are visible through 14 practice entries in eight existing views, without
changing any ordinary goal, P profile or protected subject. The complete
central report has deliberately not been rerun for this bounded successor.

The source-complete report and exact command logs are retained in the
[central closeout evidence](../goal-evidence/2026-10-18/chemie-current450-final-source-complete-central-closeout-technical-20261018-v1/).
Existing valid independent reviews remain reusable; changed routes and actual
assessment interfaces require targeted successor reviews. The current local
integration has not been committed or validated by a successor GitHub CI run.
Mathematics, Physics, Biology and Economics retain their protected M7 baselines.
Machine curriculum QA remains separate from human approval and trial.

